//BUG="a bare `ret` must be the last statement in its block"
//OUT="one"

// Not in FEEDBACK.md. `ret` with no value is only parsed correctly when
// nothing follows it in the block: the parser tries to read an expression
// after the keyword, so the next statement is consumed as the return value and
// the compile fails with "Unexpected token". Here the guarded early return is
// followed by more code, which is the normal shape of an early return.
//
// The workaround is to make the `ret` the last line of an if-block, as
// 05_functions/07_bare_return_ends_a_void_function.cpl does.

fn once
    out "one"
    ret
    out "two"

fn main
    once()
